Rules:
- For COPY references: extract the member name only (e.g., COPY CUSTFILE → "CUSTFILE")
- For CALL targets: CALL 'PROGNAME' → isDynamic=false; CALL WS-PROG-NAME → isDynamic=true
- For paragraphs: include only names from PROCEDURE DIVISION (not section headers)
- For data items: include 01-level and 77-level items only (skip subordinate levels except 88)
- For usage: extract the USAGE clause (COMP, COMP-3, BINARY, POINTER, DISPLAY); leave empty if not specified
- For conditions: extract ALL 88-level items with their parent data item and value(s)
- For parameters: extract data items from the LINKAGE SECTION; infer direction from how they are used (read-only = IN, written = OUT, both = INOUT)
- For SQL: extract from EXEC SQL ... END-EXEC blocks; targetTable is the primary table (FROM, INTO, UPDATE, DELETE FROM)
- For CICS: extract from EXEC CICS ... END-EXEC blocks
- For executionMode: CICS if program contains EXEC CICS commands; BATCH if invoked only from JCL with no CICS; BATCH_AND_CICS if both patterns present; UNKNOWN if unclear
- For fileDefinitions: infer data store type from SELECT/ASSIGN clauses and file organization. INDEXED → VSAM KSDS, SEQUENTIAL with VSAM in ASSIGN → ESDS, RELATIVE → RRDS. If no VSAM indicators, classify as FLAT_FILE
- For externalInterfaces:
  - EXEC CICS LINK → CICS_LINK
  - EXEC CICS XCTL → CICS_XCTL
  - EXEC CICS WRITEQ TS / READQ TS / DELETEQ TS → CICS_TS (NOT MQ)
  - EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD / READQ TD → CICS_TD (NOT MQ)
  - EXEC CICS START TRANSID → CICS_START
  - CALL 'MQPUT' / 'MQGET' / 'MQOPEN' / 'MQCLOSE' / 'MQCONN' / 'MQDISC' / 'MQINQ' / 'MQSET' → MQ
  - CALL 'CBLTDLI' or 'AIBTDLI' → IMS. Details should include function code (GU, GN, GHU, GNP, ISRT, DLET, REPL) and PCB/PSB name if identifiable
  - CALL to socket libraries → TCP
  - EXEC CICS READ / WRITE / REWRITE / DELETE / STARTBR / READNEXT / READPREV / ENDBR → CICS_FILE. Details should include DATASET/FILE name and operation
  - EXEC CICS ENQ / DEQ → CICS_ENQ. Details should include RESOURCE name and length
  - BIND / READY / FINISH / OBTAIN / STORE / MODIFY / ERASE / FIND / GET in DML context (CA-IDMS) → IDMS. Details should include record name and area if identifiable
  - CALL 'ADABAS' or CALL 'ADACALL' → ADABAS. Details should include command code and file number if identifiable
  - SORT or MERGE verb → SORT. Details should include sort file name and INPUT/OUTPUT PROCEDURE or USING/GIVING clause
  - CALL 'DFSORT' / 'ICETOOL' / 'IDCAMS' / 'IEBGENER' / 'IEBCOPY' → BATCH_UTIL. Details should include utility name and operation
  - Always populate the paragraph field with the paragraph name where the interface is invoked
- For dbTables: deduplicate across all SQL statements. Collect all column names and operations per table. Extract table names from FROM, JOIN, INTO, UPDATE, DELETE FROM clauses. Extract column names from SELECT lists, WHERE predicates, SET clauses, INSERT column lists. Only include tables from EXEC SQL blocks
- Return ONLY the JSON object, no markdown fences, no explanation